From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 06:18:35 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 233/638] chrome: integrate the AROS desktop shell [chromium]
 [aros]

AI_PHASE: chromium-phase-4-browser-link

AI_STATUS: done

ROOT_CAUSE: The upstream browser frame required file/icon, external URL, default-client, and app-progress platform hooks, but Linux implementations depend on XDG, D-Bus, GTK, and Unity.

FIX_REASON: Open verified native paths through workbench.library, dispatch external protocols through optional openurl.library, preserve asynchronous icon callbacks safely, and report unsupported default-client and app-icon progress capabilities without false claims.

SCOPE: chrome/browser AROS icon loader, platform utility, shell integration, download status UI, and GN registration.

VALIDATION: ninja -C out/aros-chrome -j48 obj/chrome/browser/libbrowser.a

RISK: Native file-type icon decoding and Wanderer app-icon progress are deferred; file/folder and external URL launch paths are real AROS integrations.

AI_DECISION_CHAIN: ACD-chromium-native-port-roadmap;
